WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:05.499
Your workbench says 454 kilos.

00:00:05.779 --> 00:00:09.105
But 454 kilos of what, and placed where?

00:00:09.385 --> 00:00:12.122
The three letters next to that number, UDL,

00:00:12.122 --> 00:00:16.131
decide whether your bench lasts ten years or bends in ten days.

00:00:16.731 --> 00:00:19.865
Most people read load capacity as a single number.

00:00:20.145 --> 00:00:25.431
They put a heavy press at one end, or stack everything in the middle, and wonder why the top sags.

00:00:26.031 --> 00:00:29.076
UDL means Uniformly Distributed Load.

00:00:29.356 --> 00:00:34.193
It is the weight a surface can carry when that weight is spread evenly from end to end.

00:00:34.473 --> 00:00:38.691
Concentrate the same weight on a small spot, and the safe limit drops.

00:00:39.291 --> 00:00:45.466
Furnisys Base and Scitec workbenches are rated at 454 kilos UDL.

00:00:45.746 --> 00:00:49.965
For a heavy machine, we place it over a leg frame or base cabinet,

00:00:49.965 --> 00:00:52.842
and add support rails where the span is long.

00:00:53.442 --> 00:00:57.528
So spread the load, or tell us exactly where the heavy item will sit.

00:00:57.808 --> 00:00:59.916
What is the heaviest thing on your bench today?

00:01:00.196 --> 00:01:05.638
Comment below, and watch our next video on workbench, workstation and workspace systems.

00:01:06.238 --> 00:01:10.483
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

